<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows $90.3 mln Aug 28.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows $90.3 mln Aug 28.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $90.3 million deficit on August 28 in the commercial forex market according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON AUGUST 28</p>
<p>Exports: $231.3 million</p>
<p>Imports: $191.8 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $179.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $308.9 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $90.3 million</p>
<p>AUGUST DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $4.219 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.347 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.233 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.692 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.413 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
